> Hunger can drive you down so develop an eating strategy.  If you are
> leaving behind the bodies of nutritious monsters you may be rushing down
> fast enough to get yourself killed.

Some monsters are poisonous and eating them will harm you, but you'll
starve quickly if you don't eat the safe ones.  A barbarian can eat
almost anything without permanent harm (And if you can reach either of
the two main exceptions to this rule, you don't need my help anymore),
but the game will still tell you when something you ate was poisonous.
Your pet also knows what's safe to eat, but there are a few things
it will avoid that you don't have to and vice versa. But in any case,
don't eat really old corpses; they'll kill you.

So a good idea is to play as a barbarian for awhile until you have a
good idea as to what's safe and what's not.  You may want to stick
with the barbarian even then; a lot of players got their first
ascension with a barbarian.  The valkyrie is also a good beginner
class; that's what I ascended with first.

If you're in trouble, try the #pray command.
Trouble can be anything from really low hit points, fainting from
hunger, food poisoning (not the same as poisonous corpses; if you see
FoodPois on your status line, #pray immediately or it'll kill you
in a few turns), submerged in lava, etc.  Just don't pray too often,
or your god will get annoyed.  You don't want to annoy someone who
can throw lightning bolts at you.

And most importantly, let us know whether you want to avoid
significant spoilers.  There are a lot more details about both my
advice and everyone else's that we've been leaving out to avoid
giving unwanted spoilers.  If you *do* want them, you need to let us
know.


